# ==============================================================================
# GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT SAMPLE (the dev pack)
# ==============================================================================
# The values shared by EVERY project. The gmake Makefile loads them before a
# project's own .env, which always wins.
#
# Build your copy and fill it in:
#   gmake env_global_enable
#
# That command reads this sample and those of every installed pack, and writes
# ~/.config/zsh/gmake/.env.global — adding the variables that are missing,
# never rewriting one that is already there. Run it again after adding a pack.
#
# RULE: only values shared by ALL your projects belong here — geographic and
# technical defaults, machine-level settings. Anything that identifies a
# specific project goes in that project's .env (see env.project.sample).
# ENFORCED: project-identifying variables are refused here at load time with an
# explicit error. Each pack names its own, in its pack.conf.
#
# This pack brings no shared default of its own: the three variables it reads
# (PACKAGE_NAME, DOCKER_BASE_IMAGE, DOCKER_LOCAL_IMAGE) identify one project, so
# they live in env.project.sample, next door.
# ==============================================================================
